SM(351,{"n":"Numbers 3","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Numbers 3.mp3","d":2342.2,"s":[[0.32,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[9.04,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.68,"Okay, we'll go ahead and get started."],[23.92,"We're gonna get started here in just a moment."],[25.52,"We're picking up at the beginning of Numbers chapter three."],[30.8,"One of the things about numbers that we talked about a little last time is that the book of Numbers doesn't sort of have us a single theme or even genre within it."],[45.92,"Um we've only we're only two chapters in, so those first two chapters seem to go together okay, I understand."],[51.04,"But as we keep going, you'll see there's all kinds of different stuff."],[54.72,"There's gonna be historical narrative, and we saw census data, and there's gonna be like commandments about certain things, and all this is just gonna be all sort of mixed together."],[65.72,"All that is to say, that when we're starting, that makes sort of summarizing and leading into what we're doing now a little trickier than when we're just in a narrative portion and I'm sort of doing the story so far."],[78.68,"So that means these summaries will be a little shorter, probably in a lot of the book of numbers, unless we sort of break off in the middle of something, which may happen from time to time."],[88.68,"But basically, uh in chapter one, uh, we read sort of the census data for all of the tribes except the tribe of Levi, because that census data was deliberately counting men of. fighting age"],[106.72,"So if they were gonna call up, because as we talked about in the ancient world, at this point they didn't have standing armies, they didn't really have a way to support a standing army."],[115.36,"And so when war was going to happen, all the men within a certain age range who were able-bodied got called up."],[123.44,"So they left their farms, they left wherever and went to war."],[127.52,"And so this was counting those men for those purposes, which is why the Levites weren't counted."],[133.76,"We talked about that."],[134.56,"The Levites, because they were devoted to the tabernacle, later the temple, and the priesthood."],[140.68,"They didn't go to war, unlike the men of the other tribes."],[144.4,"Then in chapter two, relatedly, we read about sort of the arrangement of of the camp, how they would sort spiral in and set up camp and then spiral out and break camp, and where the different tribes were camped around the tabernacle at the center."],[161.08,"So at the center was the tabernacle, the Levites were camped right around the tabernacle, and then the other tribes were surrounding that in sort of another ring."],[172.04,"We talked about sort of the concentric circles."],[174.92,"So tonight, for most, if not all of the night, we're going to be talking about the Levites."],[181.24,"So we sort of have talked about everybody else in detail."],[184.12,"Now, Levites have obviously been mentioned as this sort of exception last time compared to the other tribes."],[190.6,"Now, the stuff we're going to be reading tonight, starting at chapter three, is going to be focusing on the the Levites and who they were, different clans, their different jobs, census data of the Levites."],[203.54,"All that kind of stuff is where we're going tonight."],[206.9,"So with that, by way of sort of review, unless anybody has any leftover comments, questions, or observations about hair color and styling, we will pick up at the beginning of Numbers chapter three."],[221.94,"Now these are the genealogies of Aaron and Moses when the Lord spoke with Moses on Mount Sinai."],[228.34,"These are the names of the sons of Aaron, Nadab the firstborn, and Abahu, Ele Elieazzerar, and Ishamar."],[236.42,"We'll pause there."],[238.02,"Well, we don't need to pause there because it's about to say it."],[239.46,"These are the names of the sons of Aaron, the anointed priests, whom he consecrated to minister as priests"],[245.98,"Nadab and Abahu had died before the Lord when they offered strange fire before the Lord in the wilderness of Sinai, and they had no children."],[253.98,"So Eliezer and Ithamar ministered as priests with Aaron their father."],[258.86,"So that's review."],[260.94,"But so because we already read about the ordination of both sets of these sons."],[265.74,"But Eliezer is now the eldest son of Aaron."],[270.7,"So he is the one who is set to inherit the high priesthood from Aaron when Aaron dies."],[278.3,"And then Ithamar is his younger brother, who is also serving as as a a priest."],[284.42,"Again the Lord spoke to Moses, saying, Bring the tribe of Levi near, and present them before Aaron the priest, so they may minister liturgically with him."],[294.58,"They shall perform duties for him and for the children of Israel before the tabernacle of testimony, according to all the works of the tabernacle."],[302.34,"They shall also perform duties for all the furnishings of the tabernacle of testimony, and for all the children of Israel, according to all the works of the tabernacle."],[310.9,"Thus you shall assign the Levites to Aaron and his sons the priests."],[315.06,"They're given entirely to me from the children of Israel."],[318.5,"And you shall appoint Aaron and his sons over the tabernacle of testimony, and they shall guard their priesthood, and all the things related to the altar, and within the veil, but the foreigner who touches these things shall be put to death."],[329.22,"the So we have Aaron high priest, that's going to be pastor's firstborn sons."],[332.54,"Okay. We have the other people from sons from Aaron's family, who are the priests, and then we have the Levites."],[347.82,"And to the Levites, we read in Leviticus, remember, this is why it was named Leviticus, the Levite book."],[354.86,"All the sacrificial offerings, you read all the duties of the priests."],[360.06,"So, what the Levites are going to do is going to be a whole series, and we're going to get more into this in almost excruciating detail tonight."],[370.7,"All the other duties, all the practical things that go into everything that's going on around the tabernacle, all the rest of those, other than the things specifically designated to the priests in terms of offering sacrifices and those things."],[385.3,"Those are going to be the duties of the Levites, and particular Levite clans are going to have responsibilities for particular elements of it."],[396.1,"Yes, that's where this is going."],[397.62,"Oh, okay. So this is where in the book of Acts, we actually just read this on Sunday in the epistle reading."],[405.19,"Then I'll give the people when this is eventually released, sometime next year, probably, an idea of when this was recorded."],[411.43,"This is where the apostles get the idea of deacons."],[414.31,"Because the word deacon just means servant."],[416.71,"So the pattern we have in the Old Testament is you have a high priest, you then have priests, you then have the Levites performing all of these practical duties."],[427.87,"And so we begin to see already in the book of Acts, and then this gets formalized by the time you get to St."],[434.35,"Paul's Epistles, where he's going to talk about episcopy, which we now translate as bishop, and then priests, and then deacons."],[445.39,"It's going to be formalized within a few decades as a structure."],[449.47,"They're getting this structure from this."],[451.11,"The idea that you have a high priest, you have priests, and then you have Levites performing all these various functions."],[458.11,"So what happens in the book of Acts is they have this sort of crisis of, oh, some of the widows aren't getting fed."],[463.23,"of And it was kind divided along little bit racial lines, kind of, in our modern terminology."],[475.67,"This is really more about ethnic background, but in our modern terms."],[479.52,"And so this is a problem."],[480.96,"So people come to the apostles with it, and the apostles are like, well, we've got these duties we were given explicitly by Christ, that we need to carry out, and that only we are assigned to do."],[495.6,"And so we can't do that and try to handle like day-to-day food distribution among the people."],[503.76,"And it's not right that we set aside the things that we've been given to do that only we could do in order to take care of that stuff."],[508.24,"do. So we are going to choose men to that"],[514.84,"And so the idea of a deacon is an evolution of the idea of the Levites, who are clergy who are designated to perform all of these other related functions that are important, but there are things that only a priest can do, as we saw in Leviticus."],[535.08,"If the priest isn't able to offer the sacrifices because he's got to refill all the oil lamps, and he's gotta, you know, move this from here to there, and he's gotta patch the tabernacle cloth, and he's gotta, then that isn't work."],[549.56,"So you need these other people who facilitate."],[553.4,"And so that then works both ways"],[557.2,"This helps us understand the proper role of a deacon, too, in the church."],[561.78,"Which sometimes in the modern world has become, oh, we find a guy with a good voice because we like to hear him do the petitions."],[569.46,"Or if you're Russian, somebody with a really deep voice."],[572.18,"So, like when I was at Say T Cons, like they would send newly ordained deacons to serve at the monastery."],[578.42,"And it seemed to be we just want a guy with a base voice from a lot of these Russian churches because they would show up and like the Great Litany kind of sounded like the Volga Boat song."],[588.34,"Like it was just super deep."],[591.16,"U,h but anyway, so and and so a lot of times people think now, because the deacon does have a role in the divine liturgy, they just think of it as this sort of performative role of doing nice litanies, and singing well."],[607.14,"That's not actually the deacon's job."],[609.94,"The deacon's job is is this kind of facilitation, and it involves visiting people and meeting with people and helping people and works of mercy and all kinds of things."],[620.5,"Because there's certain things that only the priest can do, and he needs to be focused on those."],[625.54,"And so having a deacon then freeze the priest up to focus on those, because the deacon is helping facilitate the other things."],[634.1,"And that was part of the plan from the very beginning."],[637.68,"If you're gonna designate only these certain people can do X,Y,Z. you then need to free them up to do XYZ and not have to do fifty other things as well"],[648.28,"In the same way that God isn't having them farm in addition to being priests."],[654.36,"They need to be focused on that."],[656.04,"So this is part of that facilitation."],[659.32,"Verse 11 Moreover, the Lord spoke to Moses, saying, Now behold, I myself have taken the Levites from among the children of Israel, instead of every firstborn who opens the womb among the children of Israel, the Levites shall be a ransom from them, therefore they shall be mine."],[674.52,"Because all the firstborn are mine."],[676.2,"On the day I struck all the firstborn in the land of Egypt, I sanctified to myself all the firstborn in Israel, from man to cattle, they shall be mine, I am the Lord."],[685.4,"So remember this."],[686.6,"This is a flashback to Exodus."],[689.36,"Remember? We were about the dedication of the firstborn after this, after the Passover."],[695.28,"Now, just to make sure someone's not misinterpreting this, by someone I might be referring to the Orthodox Study Bible notes."],[702.89,"This is not saying that like God wanted to kill the firstborn of Israel just like the firstborn of Egypt."],[710.57,"Because why would he?"],[714.09,"What this is saying is why did God kill theed firstborn of Egypt?"],[720.49,"But the Egyptians killed the firstborn."],[723.29,"Because the Egyptians were murdering all of the."],[728.53,"We're murdering all of the Hebrew children."],[730.35,"At the beginning of the book of Exodus."],[731.47,"The sons in particular"],[734.69,"The daughters could marry an Egyptian man and they could kind of get rid of the Hebrews that way."],[741.33,"But the su get rid of all the sons."],[743.49,"So they were actively murdering all of the males."],[746.85,"And so by God executing justice for that, what God was saying was those children you Egyptians killed weren't just the children of some slaves."],[758.77,"Those were my children."],[767.41,"This is important to understand because this God's going to use this language later."],[773.65,"Because unfortunately, child sacrifice was a real thing in the ancient Near East."],[775.97,"That happened a lot, especially among the Phoenicians"],[783.21,"Sorry, Lebanese listeners."],[786.49,"But it was a real thing."],[789.21,"And God is going to condemn it and say, You sacrificed my children."],[797.29,"He's going to say this to the Israelites when they sacrificed, quote unquote, their own children."],[802.49,"God's going to say, those were my children, not yours."],[806.33,"I entrusted them to you."],[807.93,"So that's what God is saying here."],[810.73,"God is saying, they belong to me."],[814.17,"I demonstrated that they belong to me when the Passover happened."],[820.09,"And I executed justice against Egypt."],[820.97,"And so they belong to me going forward"],[827.33,"Don't you forget it either, Israel."],[830.77,"Your sons are not yours to do whatever you want to with them."],[834.69,"And your children in general."],[836.61,"This is an important principle."],[838.31,"That continues to this day."],[839.83,"When God gives people children, he's really entrusting some children of his, because they belong to him, to those people."],[848.71,"And those people are going to be held accountable for what they do with regards to those children."],[854.39,"That's not fundamentally different than a lot of other things that God gives people."],[858.63,"When God gives us, God gives us money, if God gives us wealth, he's going to hold us accountable for what we do with it."],[863.43,"If he gives us time on this earth, he's going to hold us. accountable for what we do with it"],[868.03,"But children, we're told over and over and over again in the Bible, are especially precious to God."],[876.27,"Because all the things we're finding out now, because all of a sudden we figured out that psychology is a discipline and stuff, about how what happens to people when they're children affects them for the rest of their lives."],[887.81,"God knew that already."],[889.01,"God knew that from the beginning."],[891.01,"And so this is a very important thing."],[893.97,"And he's saying he could, if he wanted to, make every firstborn son in Israel a priest."],[901.18,"Because they all belong to him."],[902.78,"He's saying, I've chosen not to do that, but just the Levites."],[908.14,"Just the Levites."],[910.9,"The father can do anything he wants with children."],[913.4,"Is that pretty much the way it was in other culture?"],[917.16,"Yes. Yeah. The Roman Potter Familius was pretty much by and large I mean, they formalized in Roman law the way things pretty much worked in the ancient Near East."],[927.8,"So i in in Roman law, the Potter Familius, when someone in the big extended family household, which included the slaves, which included the had a baby, they would go and present the baby to the Potter Familius, and he would decide whether it got to live or not."],[944.46,"Like, that's the level of."],[946.9,"And you have to combine that with the reality that there was no concept of sexual consent in the ancient world."],[952.62,"People th thougoughtht they they. it wasn't just slaves that they owned"],[957.14,"Children, it was women, it was, and who they could do with as they pleased, and God is very much correcting that."],[964.9,"Like, no. That's all those people actually belong to God, not to any guy on earth."],[973.54,"Verse 14. Furthermore, I like how they tried to vary up the interest."],[979.14,"We had a more over, and now we have a furthermore."],[982.5,"Furthermore, the Lord spoke to Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, saying, Number the children of Levi by their fathers's houses, by their tribes, and by their families."],[992.5,"You shall number every male from a month old and above."],[996.26,"Okay, so now notice this census is different."],[998.74,"Remember, the previous census was 20 years old or older"],[999.5,"This is just every male who's a month old or older."],[1006.22,"But as we talked about, that's because that was for military service."],[1009.58,"One month olds can't serve in the military."],[1012.78,"At least not for very long."],[1016.38,"But that's not what this is for."],[1019.28,"This is about priesthood and Levitical responsibilities."],[1024.4,"So Moses and Aaron numbered them according to the voice of the Lord and the manner the Lord commanded them."],[1029.36,"These are the sons of Levi by their names, Gershon, Kohat, and Morari."],[1034.56,"Okay, the sons of Levi, this is not talking about uh literal sons of the person Levi, who was the son of Jacob, who is not alive at this point."],[1043.68,"The sons of Levi, these are sort of three big clans"],[1049.24,"The Levites basically are made up of these three big clans, and then there's sort of sub clans of families within each one of those."],[1058.28,"So that's what this is talking about."],[1060.6,"Sort of big family groups."],[1063.08,"If you're like if you look at a family tree, you got big, big groups."],[1068.04,"So there's these three big groups Gershon, Kohat, and Morari."],[1072.44,"These are the names of the sons of Gershon by their tribes, Libni and Shimeh, and the sons of Kohat by their families, Amram, Izahar, Hebron, and Uziel, and the sons of Morari by their families, Mali and Mushi."],[1086.28,"You never see a kid named Mushi anymore."],[1088.28,"These are the tribes of the Levites by their father's houses"],[1089.12,"Not one Mushi I ever baptized."],[1095.28,"Okay, so now we're we're breaking down into sort of bigger clan groups and families."],[1101.44,"Of course, people don't have last names at this time in history."],[1105.12,"From Gershon came the tribe of the Libnites and the Shemites."],[1109.36,"These are the families of the Gershonites."],[1111.68,"Their census, according to the number of all the males from a month old and above, was seven thousand five hundred."],[1117.6,"The children of the Gershonites were to camp behind the tabernacle along the west side, and the ruler of the father's house of the tribe of Gershon was Eliasaph, the son of Lael."],[1127.36,"So remember chapters one and two, we got each tribe, and then chapter two, we got where they camped."],[1133.6,"Remember, we said the Levites are in this, are surrounding the tabernacle"],[1138.52,"So this is telling us where that family was in relation to the tabernacle in that sort of inner circle where the Levites are camped."],[1146.76,"All of this is ordered."],[1163.64,"So we're also getting now sort of what their assignment was in terms of what they were responsible to take care of."],[1171.0,"So in this case, in the wilderness, taking care of it meant a couple things."],[1175.24,"Number one, literally taking care of it, mending it, repairing it, making sure it remained intact and functional, but also taking it down and putting it back up when they broke camp and when they made camp again."],[1188.24,"From Kohat came the tribes of the Amramites, the Isarites, the Hebronites, and the Uzielites."],[1195.6,"These are the tribes of the Kohatites."],[1197.84,"Their census, according to the number of all the males from a month old and above, was 8,600, keeping charge of the holy things."],[1204.96,"The tribes of the children of Kohat were to camp along the south side of the tabernacle, and the ruler of the house of the families of the Kohathite tribes was Eleaziphan, the son of Uzil."],[1215.76,"Their charge included the ark, the table, the lampstand, the altars, the utensils of the holy place, with which they ministered liturgically. the screen and all their works"],[1225.88,"Now the ruler over the rulers of the Levites was Eliezer, the son of Aaron the priest."],[1231.72,"He was appointed to be in charge of those responsible for the holy things."],[1235.48,"So Aaron's family is part of one of these groups."],[1241.08,"And so the person who's the heir to be the high priest is sort of in charge of this segment of the Levites."],[1248.92,"These are the ones who are in charge of sort of all the accoutrement of the tabernacle, all the stuff, including the Ark of the Covenant, all these things that had wherever we read they had all had poles that you could insert to carry them."],[1262.2,"So they were the ones who broke that down and set that up and then maintained everything."],[1268.04,"From Morari come the tribe of the Malites and the tribe of the Mushites."],[1273.36,"These were the tribes of Morari."],[1275.6,"Their census, according to the number of all the males from a month old and above, was 6,500."],[1280.48,"And the ruler of the house of the families of the Morari tribe was Zuriel, the son of Abihal."],[1285.84,"These were to camp on the north side of the tabernacle."],[1288.48,"The appointed duty of the children of Morari included the pillars of the tabernacle, and the bars, the columns, and the bases, and all their furnishings and works, and the pillars of the court all around with their bases, pegs, and cords."],[1300.02,"So they're in charge of the pole, basically the poles that hold everything up in the slots in the ground, breaking that down, setting it up, maintaining, maintaining all of those things."],[1311.54,"Those camped in front of the tabernacle of testimony on the east were Moses, Aaron, and his sons, performing the guard duties of the holy place on behalf of the children of Israel."],[1321.34,"But the foreigner who touches these things shall be put to death."],[1339.9,"Remember, a big part of their duty is this protective duty."],[1344.62,"And again, this is something people tend to misread."],[1347.5,"People tend to misread this as, well, we don't want those dirty foreigners or non Levites to get their hands on these things because they'll dirty up these things."],[1357.02,"things. They are not protecting the holy from those people"],[1361.86,"They are protecting those people from the holy things."],[1366.1,"Because Rebra Day Dab and Abuhu, someone who is not holy, who has not prepared themselves, who has not done the things that they're supposed to do, approaches God in the wrong way, it is incredibly dangerous for them."],[1382.58,"This is why, remember when Adam and Eve were put out of paradise."],[1388.26,"There's a cherub with a flaming sword put there to keep them out."],[1394.26,"Why? Because God didn't want them to sneak back in, like he couldn't do anything about it."],[1399.06,"No, because if they tried to come back in in their sinful state, bad things would happen to them."],[1402.82,"God They had to be protected from being in's presence until they had repented and prepared themselves."],[1413.66,"That's why we have this life in this world."],[1415.66,"That's the picture we're being given in Genesis."],[1417.74,"So at the end of their lives, Adam and Eve, hopefully, having spent a life of repentance, were then prepared to come into the presence of God again."],[1425.66,"That's the idea."],[1427.5,"This is where St."],[1429.42,"Paul, we talked about this back in 1 Corinthians, but this is why St."],[1433.1,"Paul gives the warning about the Eucharist that people have got had gotten sick and even died because they weren't preparing themselves properly to come into the presence of God."],[1444.78,"There was sort of this whiplash."],[1447.27,"So St. Paul is on one hand having to deal with a group of Jewish Christians who are saying, well, no, if the Gentiles want to come to the Eucharist, they need to keep the whole Torah."],[1458.85,"They need to become Jewish, they need to be circumcised, they need to keep kosher, and they need to do all these things."],[1463.57,"Otherwise, they're not prepared."],[1465.11,"And St. Paul vehemently argues against that."],[1468.47,"Says, no, they've been baptized into Christ, they've put on Christ, they can approach."],[1473.51,"But then there's the other extreme."],[1475.35,"The other extreme is, oh, just don't worry about it, come as you are."],[1478.87,"And treating the Eucharist, treating Christ casually, which St."],[1484.31,"Paul is saying, that's dangerous on the other side."],[1488.15,"So there is a proper way for St."],[1490.47,"Paul for a non-Jewish Christian to prepare to receive the Eucharist."],[1492.23,"That's not the way to do it"],[1494.43,"That's just not keeping the Jewish regulations."],[1498.99,"But there is a way to do it."],[1500.27,"And it is necessary."],[1501.47,"Because otherwise, why?"],[1502.75,"It's dangerous for the person."],[1507.79,"And this is why when a priest is ordained in the Orthodox Church to this day, the bishop charges us with words very similar to this that we're reading here in Numbers."],[1518.75,"And we have the lamb for communion put in our hands, and we're told to protect it."],[1525.07,"Not that giving it to the wrong person is going to do something bad to Christ, like Christ is Christ."],[1532.83,"We're not trying, we don't have to protect God from anything, but we're protecting people. from what could happen if they're approaching it in an inappropriate way"],[1543.35,"So this is why we don't just give communion to anybody who walks in the door."],[1549.83,"And this is really misunderstood, I know, by people who aren't Orthodox."],[1555.43,"People who aren't Orthodox think we're really exclusive and we're not loving and we're not welcoming because we don't give you communion."],[1562.63,"But let me be very blunt about this."],[1564.55,"If I hated people, I would be an ecumenist."],[1570.47,"And I would give communion to anyone who walked up, and I wouldn't care, and I'd give it to them week after week, and I never talked to them about anything, and I would just do that, and all of that would be heaping condemnation on them."],[1582.23,"I would go to hell too"],[1588.52,"For hating people that much and doing that."],[1592.04,"But that's why ecumenism is a heresy, and we call it anathema."],[1596.76,"Because it's not actually loving."],[1602.36,"It's the opposite."],[1603.96,"It's indifference to people."],[1605.86,"And so that just like then, now, part of the job of the priest is making that discernment."],[1616.42,"Not of who is worthy, nobody's worthy."],[1618.99,"That's why right before, right before the Eucharist, we say, I say holy things are for the holy."],[1624.59,"And what does the choir respond? with"],[1626.39,"Well, there's only one who's holy."],[1628.55,"Christ. It is the only one who's really holy."],[1631.43,"So I'm not just giving communion to the holy people."],[1634.17,"Or the worthy people, because there aren't any of those."],[1636.41,"It's an adverb."],[1638.09,"It's people who are approaching worthily, meaning they're approaching with repentance."],[1642.65,"They're approaching with faithfulness as best they can."],[1646.35,"They're approaching in order to be healed for what's happened to them and what they've done."],[1651.31,"And that discernment is part of the priest's job, which is also why, which is also why, and I like to reemphasize this over and over again, you guys are not allowed to excommunicate yourselves."],[1665.55,"Meaning, you're not allowed to decide to for yourself whether you receive communion on a given Sunday."],[1670.11,"You don't have the right to excommunicate people"],[1671.75,"That's pride. That's arrogance."],[1676.15,"You're not a priest, you're not a bishop."],[1678.55,"That includes yourself."],[1681.35,"There are some people out there who are sort of proud and arrogant and need someone to come and convict them of their sin."],[1688.23,"But there are a lot of other people who are very tender hearted and very aware of their own sin."],[1693.99,"Who need someone to come to them over and over again and say, You're forgiven."],[1699.99,"Christ has forgiven you."],[1701.43,"God loves you."],[1702.31,"There are people who need to hear that too."],[1704.71,"And so the people who tend to excommunicate themselves are the latter group."],[1709.51,"The former group will not fast and not do anything and come and receive communion anyway."],[1714.31,"It's a whole separate thing."],[1715.73,"But the people who are more tender-hearted, they're the ones who tend to excommunicate themselves, and they need someone to say, you know what?"],[1724.37,"Christ loves you."],[1725.65,"He wants to give himself to you in the Eucharist this Sunday."],[1729.57,"Don't cut yourself off from that."],[1732.05,"The core is in the Orthodox Church, we aren't governed by rules."],[1736.13,"We're governed by people who use rules as a tool."],[1741.25,"In a lot of cases, though, how this is boils down in practice varies a lot."],[1748.13,"In segments, we'll say of Roman Catholicism, it's governed by rules."],[1752.05,"There's canon law."],[1753.11,"And these are the this is it."],[1754.64,"And you can research it and find out."],[1756.4,"This is it."],[1757.44,"And then in some segments of Protestantism, there just are no rules."],[1759.12,"Everything is just purely, everything is just purely relational"],[1765.08,"And the rules are sort of made up, you know, for people."],[1767.82,"They're ad hoc, yeah."],[1770.22,"And of this is part of the issue is that people who come into the Orthodox Church try to approach it as well, I can go and read books and research and learn all the rules."],[1779.98,"You can't. Because that's not how the Orthodox Church works."],[1784.22,"And if you try and approach it that way, you end up being one of these weird cranks on the internet who's going around saying none of the bishops are really Orthodox because they don't follow the rules."],[1792.94,"So the collection of canons in the Orthodox Church, the name of that book is The Rudder."],[1798.7,"Like the rudder of a boat."],[1801.26,"Because the canons, the rules are a tool that the bishop uses to guide the church and its people."],[1810.1,"So you can't find out for yourself."],[1813.14,"And part of this excommunicating yourself comes from, well, I went and looked up the rules, and now I'm going to apply those rules to myself."],[1820.18,"But you're not the proper person to apply the rules."],[1823.94,"And this parish, I am, or the bishop."],[1826.6,"If he's here, or if I'm messing up, you need to talk to him."],[1831.22,"But he's the final authority."],[1833.46,"But. Um, but that's the person who applies the rules."],[1838.95,"Because if we plu try to apply the rules to ourselves, we fall into those extremes of either cutting ourselves a lot of slack or not cutting ourselves any slack, and you need someone else to help you navigate that."],[1856.83,"But what's important here, this is from the very beginning."],[1859.07,"We're in the Torah."],[1860.95,"God set up all of these things to be administered through humans to other humans."],[1867.19,"And the the through whom there are the people he put in a position of authority."],[1872.79,"Not as Christ points out, to lord it over them."],[1875.67,"The high priest wasn't walking around the camp like like, I'm the high priest."],[1879.67,"Yes. In fact, when he was walking around the camp, he was dressed just like everybody else, by the way."],[1884.87,"He only put the vestments on when he was in the tabernacle."],[1888.39,"But to be the one, because God knows how we're built, because he built us, we need someone outside of ourselves to advise us these things."],[1900.03,"None of these things were just left up to the individual Israelites."],[1903.15,"There's a period of time we're going to get to in the Old Testament where everyone just does what is right in their own eyes, and that's not going to be a good time."],[1911.23,"It's going to be a really horrible time to live in Israel."],[1914.83,"God entrusts these things to certain people, and then God holds those people accountable for what they do with that gift of that role that God gave to them."],[1925.63,"Verse 40. Again the Lord said to Moses, Take a census of all the firstborn males of the children of Israel from a month old and above, and take the number of their names."],[1935.63,"You shall take the Levites for me, I am the Lord, instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel, and the cattle of the Levites instead of all the firstborn cattle among the children of Israel."],[1945.43,"So Moses took a census of all the firstborn among the children of Israel, in the manner the Lord commanded him."],[1950.95,"Thus all the firstborn males, according to the number of names from a month old and above, from the census were twenty-two thousand two hundred and seventy-three."],[1959.67,"Then the Lord spoke to Moses, saying, Take the Levites instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel, and the cattle of the Levites instead of their cattle, the Levites shall be mine, I am the Lord."],[1969.75,"But for well, we'll pause there."],[1971.59,"So, what's all this about?"],[1973.51,"God is saying that the Levites have this kind of firstborn status."],[1979.03,"Remember, firstborn is a status among the tribes of Israel."],[1984.35,"Levi, not the firstborn son."],[1988.35,"Third. Okay. But remember, Reuben and Simeon both got disowned."],[1994.19,"So the Levites have this firstborn status."],[1999.07,"That's why they're the priests."],[2000.83,"And so he's saying the idea here with this census is he's pointing out the numbers are roughly the same."],[2007.23,"The number of Levite males and the number of firstborn males for the whole of Israel is roughly the same."],[2015.23,"And so God is saying that firstborn status goes to the Levites."],[2020.03,"So hypothetically, if he hadn't done this, the firstborn sons would be priests."],[2026.43,"We came to that earlier"],[2027.09,"Which was, remember, that was the old pattern."],[2031.45,"When we talked about the golden calf."],[2033.29,"Before that episode, sacrifices, there was no priesthood per se."],[2039.37,"Sacrifices were offered by the fathers of families and the heads of clans."],[2043.37,"So, like, think of Job."],[2045.45,"Job is there offering sacrifices for his children and their families."],[2050.25,"Part of his job as the head of the clan."],[2053.29,"Or Abraham offering sacrifices, Isaac offering sacrifices, Jacob offering sacrifices."],[2058.49,"It was the head of the family who had that role."],[2062.09,"And the firstborn son is the one who inherited that role and performed the uh sacrifice, those priestly duties."],[2071.81,"So that status and then assignment of the priestly duties, is is part of what's going on with Levi being designated as the firstborn."],[2080.47,"So those are no longer any of these other people supposed to be performing sacrifices and performing those duties."],[2088.95,"Those duties are all given to the tribe of Levi."],[2092.71,"That's not necessarily what's going to happen."],[2094.55,"We're gonna see as we go forward in the Old Testament."],[2096.95,"We're gonna see some people work around that, like hiring Levites to do sacrifices to idols."],[2102.15,"There's gonna be all kinds of workarounds people try to do."],[2105.27,"But that's that's what's going on here."],[2108.15,"And so sort of the census numbering is sort of performing this sort of symbolic function, which is another reason why. precise numbers"],[2118.19,"We've got these big round numbers."],[2119.56,"Precise numbers are not really that necessary to make the point that we're trying to make here."],[2124.44,"Verse 46. But for the redemption of the 273 firstborn from the children of Israel who are more in number than the Levites, you shall take five shekels for each one individually."],[2134.36,"You shall take them according to the holy de Drachma, the twenty oboe of the shekel."],[2140.36,"Then you shall give the silver with which the excess number of them is redeemed to Aaron and his sons."],[2145.24,"So Moses took the silver, the redemption of those who exceeded the number for the redemption of the Levites."],[2150.76,"From the firstborn of the children of Israel, he took the silver, 1,375 and 65 shekels according to the holy shekel."],[2157.88,"Then Moses gave their redemption money for those in excess to Aaron and his sons according to the voice of the Lord and the manner the Lord commanded Moses."],[2165.68,"So this is basically the origin for what's going to become the temple tax."],[2171.44,"Meaning, and this is being instituted here, even though money is not super important when they're living in a camp in the desert."],[2177.92,"Like, what are you gonna do with silver, really?"],[2180.08,"But will become important once they're settled in the land and commerce and things are going on."],[2185.2,"In addition to just, hey, we're bringing sacrifices and you get to eat the meat or the wheat cakes or whatever, and these kind of things."],[2193.44,"There's gonna be expenditures and stuff required."],[2196.32,"Times when things need to be fixed, times when gold needs to be added to gold plating and repaired, and things like this."],[2203.2,"That's gonna require money."],[2205.8,"And so this is a means by which a certain amount of money based on firstborn sons, therefore, bigger families are gonna pay more, smaller families less."],[2218.14,"To sort of the upkeep of the tabernacle."],[2221.58,"Now, this is going to get abused."],[2224.3,"I know you're shocked."],[2226.46,"But the biggest abuse of this is gonna come in the New Testament during Jesus' earthly ministry."],[2233.66,"We've talked about this before when we were in the Gospels, but at that point in history, 70% of the land in Judea that wasn't owned by the Romans, that wasn't like directly administered by the Romans, 70% of it belonged to the high priest's family."],[2248.94,"Because the Romans. let them do a temple tax"],[2253.22,"And so they would deliberately overtax people, forcing them to sell their land to the high priest's family in order to pay the temple tax, and then basically pay them slave wages, basically, to then work what had been their own family's land."],[2271.86,"We're going to see later in the book of Numbers, every single family is going to get a piece of land given to them by God."],[2279.94,"And remember, we read about the Sabbath years of the Jubilee and how it was all supposed to always stay with that family."],[2286.02,"The high priest family decided they wanted to take 70% of it."],[2289.22,"And we're probably after the other 30."],[2291.22,"They just hadn't pulled it off yet."],[2292.74,"And then the temple got destroyed and things went very badly for them."],[2294.74,"But so that became something that was abused"],[2299.02,"But initially, this was not set up as a way for the priests to enrich themselves."],[2304.78,"This was set up as a way for the necessary elements of the life of the tabernacle to keep functioning, beyond just in kind bartering kind of things."],[2315.92,"Of food and things being given to the priests."],[2318.88,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2326.24,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2331.6,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.68,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: Numbers has no single theme","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Picking up at the beginning of <b>Numbers 3</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Numbers has no single <b>theme or genre</b></li><li class=\"d1\">first two chapters seem to go together; after that, all kinds of stuff</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>historical narrative</b>, <b>census data</b>, <b>commandments</b> - all mixed together</li><li class=\"d0\">Harder to summarize and lead in than a pure narrative → <b>summaries will be shorter</b>, unless we break off mid-something</li></ul>"},{"t":88.68,"lv":3,"h":"Recap of chapters 1-2, and tonight","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Ch. 1</b>: census of all tribes <b>except Levi</b></li><li class=\"d1\">counted men of <b>fighting age</b> - no <b>standing armies</b>, men left farms and went to war</li><li class=\"d1\">Levites <b>devoted to the tabernacle</b>, later temple, and priesthood → no war</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Ch. 2</b>: camp arrangement</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>spiral in</b> to set up camp, spiral out to break camp</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>tabernacle at center</b>, Levites right around it, other tribes in another ring - concentric circles</li><li class=\"d0\">Tonight (most if not all): the <b>Levites</b></li><li class=\"d1\">who they were, <b>different clans</b>, their <b>jobs</b>, <b>census data</b></li></ul>"},{"t":221.94,"lv":2,"h":"3:1-4 - The sons of Aaron","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Genealogies of <b>Aaron and Moses</b>\" when the Lord spoke on <b>Mount Sinai</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Sons of Aaron: <b>Nadab</b> (firstborn), <b>Abihu</b>, <b>Eleazar</b>, <b>Ithamar</b></li><li class=\"d1\">anointed priests, consecrated to minister</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Nadab and Abihu</b> died offering <b>strange fire</b> in Sinai - no children</li><li class=\"d0\">Review: ordination of both sets of sons already read</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Eleazar</b> now eldest → <b>inherits the high priesthood</b> when Aaron dies</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Ithamar</b> his younger brother, also a priest</li></ul>"},{"t":284.42,"lv":2,"h":"3:5-10 - Levites assigned to Aaron","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Bring the tribe of Levi near\" - present them to <b>Aaron</b> to <b>minister liturgically with him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">perform duties for him and for Israel at the tabernacle and <b>all its furnishings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"given entirely to me\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Aaron and sons appointed over the tabernacle - guard the <b>priesthood</b>, the altar, within the <b>veil</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>foreigner who touches shall be put to death</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Structure: <b>high priest</b> (Aaron, then firstborn sons) → <b>priests</b> (Aaron's family) → <b>Levites</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Leviticus (\"the Levite book\") = sacrificial offerings, priests' duties</li><li class=\"d1\">Levites: <b>all the other practical duties</b> around the tabernacle</li><li class=\"d1\">particular <b>Levite clans</b> get particular elements - \"excruciating detail tonight\"</li></ul>"},{"t":397.62,"lv":3,"h":"Origin of deacons in Acts","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Read on Sunday in the epistle reading - Acts</li><li class=\"d1\">(dating this recording for the release next year)</li><li class=\"d0\">Apostles get the idea of <b>deacons</b> here - <i>deacon</i> = <b>servant</b></li><li class=\"d0\">OT pattern: high priest, priests, <b>Levites with practical duties</b></li><li class=\"d1\">formalized by Paul's epistles: <i>episkopos</i> (bishop), <b>priests</b>, <b>deacons</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"within a few decades\" - they get the structure from <b>this</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Acts: <b>widows not getting fed</b> - divided along ethnic lines (\"racial\" in modern terms)</li><li class=\"d1\">apostles: duties given <b>explicitly by Christ</b>, only we can do them</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not right\" to set them aside for <b>day-to-day food distribution</b> → choose men for that</li><li class=\"d0\">Deacon = evolution of the <b>Levites</b></li><li class=\"d1\">clergy for related functions that are important</li><li class=\"d1\">priest can't offer sacrifices if refilling <b>oil lamps</b>, moving things, <b>patching the cloth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">need others who <b>facilitate</b></li></ul>"},{"t":557.2,"lv":3,"h":"The proper role of the deacon","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Helps us understand the deacon's role in the church</li><li class=\"d0\">Modern: \"find a guy with a good voice\" for the petitions</li><li class=\"d1\">Russian: \"deep voice\" - at St. Tikhon's newly ordained deacons sent to the monastery; <b>Great Litany sounded like the Volga Boat Song</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not the deacon's job - not a <b>performative role</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Real job: <b>facilitation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">visiting people, meeting people, helping, <b>works of mercy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">certain things only a priest can do → deacon <b>frees him up</b> to focus</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Part of the plan from the very beginning\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God isn't having priests <b>farm</b> in addition</li></ul>"},{"t":659.32,"lv":2,"h":"3:11-13 - The Levites for the firstborn","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">God has taken the Levites <b>instead of every firstborn</b> that opens the womb</li><li class=\"d1\">Levites = a <b>ransom</b>, \"they shall be mine\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"All the firstborn are mine\" - sanctified the day he <b>struck the firstborn of Egypt</b>, man and cattle</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Flashback to Exodus</b>: dedication of the firstborn after Passover</li></ul>"},{"t":695.28,"lv":3,"h":"\"Those were my children\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not (as some study-Bible notes might read it) that God wanted to kill Israel's firstborn like Egypt's</li><li class=\"d0\">Why did God kill Egypt's firstborn? <b>Egyptians were murdering the Hebrew sons</b></li><li class=\"d1\">daughters could marry Egyptians and \"get rid of the Hebrews that way\"</li><li class=\"d1\">so they killed <b>all the males</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God's justice: those weren't just \"children of some slaves\" - <b>\"those were my children\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same language later against <b>child sacrifice</b></li><li class=\"d1\">real in the ancient Near East, especially <b>Phoenicians</b> - \"Sorry, Lebanese listeners\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God to Israel: <b>\"you sacrificed my children\"</b>, \"I entrusted them to you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Passover shows they <b>belong to me</b> - \"don't you forget it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Principle to this day: <b>children entrusted</b> by God → <b>accountable</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like money, wealth, time on earth</li><li class=\"d1\">children <b>especially precious</b> to God</li><li class=\"d1\">psychology \"figured out\" how childhood shapes people for life - <b>God knew from the beginning</b></li><li class=\"d0\">He could have made <b>every firstborn son a priest</b> - chose <b>just the Levites</b></li></ul>"},{"t":910.9,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: fathers' authority in other cultures","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: Father could do anything with children - same in other cultures?</li><li class=\"d0\">Yes - <b>Roman <i>pater familias</i></b>; Roman law formalized how the ancient Near East worked</li><li class=\"d1\">baby in the extended household (<b>slaves</b> included) presented to the <i>pater familias</i> → <b>he decided if it lived</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Plus: <b>no concept of sexual consent</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just slaves - <b>children, women</b> owned, to do with as pleased</li><li class=\"d0\">God <b>correcting</b> that: \"No\" - they belong to <b>God</b>, not any man</li></ul>"},{"t":973.54,"lv":2,"h":"3:14-20 - Census of the Levites","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Furthermore\" - he likes the varied wording</li><li class=\"d0\">Number Levi's sons <b>by fathers' houses, tribes, families</b>: <b>every male a month old and up</b></li><li class=\"d1\">different from <b>20 and up</b> - that was <b>military service</b></li><li class=\"d1\">this one is for <b>priesthood and Levitical responsibilities</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses and Aaron number them as commanded</li><li class=\"d0\">Sons of Levi: <b>Gershon, Kohath, Merari</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not literal sons of Levi (long dead) - <b>three big clans</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sub-clans of families under each - big groups on a family tree</li><li class=\"d1\">Gershon: <b>Libni, Shimei</b>; Kohath: <b>Amram, Izhar, Hebron, Uzziel</b>; Merari: <b>Mahli, Mushi</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"never see a kid named Mushi anymore\" - \"not one I ever baptized\"</li><li class=\"d0\">No last names at this time</li></ul>"},{"t":1105.12,"lv":2,"h":"3:21-37 - The three clans and their jobs","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Gershonites</b> (Libnites, Shimeites): <b>7,500</b></li><li class=\"d1\">camp <b>behind the tabernacle, west</b>; ruler <b>Eliasaph son of Lael</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ch. 2 told where tribes camped; now where each Levite family sits in the <b>inner circle</b> - \"all of this is ordered\"</li><li class=\"d1\">also their <b>assignment</b> - what they care for</li><li class=\"d1\">in the wilderness: <b>mending, repairing</b>, keeping it intact - and <b>taking down / putting up</b> at camp changes</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Kohathites</b> (Amramites, Izharites, Hebronites, Uzzielites): <b>8,600</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>south side</b>; ruler <b>Elizaphan son of Uzziel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">charge: <b>ark, table, lampstand, altars, utensils of the holy place, screen</b></li><li class=\"d1\">over the rulers: <b>Eleazar son of Aaron</b> - in charge of those over the holy things</li><li class=\"d1\">heir to the high priesthood oversees this segment</li><li class=\"d1\">the items had <b>poles</b> for carrying → they broke down, set up, maintained</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Merarites</b> (Mahlites, Mushites): <b>6,500</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>north side</b>; ruler <b>Zuriel son of Abihail</b></li><li class=\"d1\">charge: <b>pillars, bars, columns, bases</b>, court pillars, <b>pegs and cords</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the \"poles that hold everything up\" - break down, set up, maintain</li></ul>"},{"t":1311.54,"lv":2,"h":"3:38-39 - Guarding the holy: protecting people","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Moses, Aaron, and his sons</b> camp in front, on the <b>east</b>, guarding the holy place for Israel</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>foreigner who touches shall be put to death</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Big part of their duty: <b>protective</b> - commonly misread</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"keep out dirty foreigners / non-Levites who would dirty the holy things\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>protecting those people from the holy things</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Nadab and Abihu</b>: unprepared, approaching God wrongly → <b>incredibly dangerous</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Adam and Eve</b>: <b>cherub with flaming sword</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not because God couldn't stop them sneaking in</li><li class=\"d1\">coming back <b>sinful</b> → bad things; protected until they <b>repented and prepared</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"why we have this life in this world\"; end of life, prepared to enter God's presence</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Paul, 1 Corinthians</b>: warning on the <b>Eucharist</b> - some sick, even died, <b>not preparing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"whiplash\": Jewish Christians say Gentiles must <b>keep the whole Torah</b> - circumcision, kosher → Paul argues <b>vehemently</b> against; baptized into Christ, \"put on Christ\"</li><li class=\"d1\">other extreme: <b>\"come as you are\"</b>, treating Christ casually → also dangerous</li><li class=\"d1\">there <b>is</b> a proper way for non-Jewish Christians to prepare - not Jewish regulations</li><li class=\"d0\">At ordination the bishop charges the priest in words similar to Numbers</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>lamb for communion</b> put in our hands: \"protect it\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not protecting Christ - <b>protecting people</b> approaching inappropriately</li></ul>"},{"t":1543.35,"lv":3,"h":"Why not communion for everyone","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Why we don't give communion to anyone who walks in</li><li class=\"d1\">misunderstood: non-Orthodox think <b>exclusive, unloving</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Blunt: <b>\"If I hated people, I would be an ecumenist\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">give communion to all, week after week, never talk → <b>heaping condemnation</b> on them</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I would go to hell too\"</li><li class=\"d1\">why <b>ecumenism is a heresy</b> - <b>indifference</b> to people, not love</li><li class=\"d0\">Priest's job: <b>discernment</b> - not who is worthy, \"nobody's worthy\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>\"Holy things are for the holy\"</b> → only <b>Christ</b> is holy</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>worthily</b> is an <b>adverb</b> - approaching with <b>repentance</b>, faithfulness, to be <b>healed</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1651.31,"lv":3,"h":"Don't excommunicate yourself","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"You are not allowed to excommunicate yourselves\"</b> - not deciding for yourself on a given Sunday</li><li class=\"d1\">pride, arrogance - includes yourself</li><li class=\"d0\">Two kinds of people</li><li class=\"d1\">proud, arrogant → need to be <b>convicted</b> (they don't fast yet commune anyway)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>tender-hearted</b>, aware of sin → need to hear <b>\"Christ has forgiven you, God loves you\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the tender ones excommunicate themselves: \"Don't cut yourself off from that\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Orthodox Church \"<b>not governed by rules</b>\" but by <b>people who use rules as a tool</b></li><li class=\"d1\">some Roman Catholic segments: rules, <b>canon law</b></li><li class=\"d1\">some Protestant segments: no rules, <b>ad hoc</b>, purely relational</li><li class=\"d1\">converts: \"read the books, learn all the rules\" → <b>internet cranks</b> saying no bishop is Orthodox</li><li class=\"d1\">canon collection = <b><i>The Rudder</i></b> - tool the bishop uses to <b>guide</b> the church</li><li class=\"d0\">You apply rules to yourself → <b>too much slack or none</b>; the priest or bishop applies them; <b>bishop final authority</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1856.83,"lv":3,"h":"God administers through humans","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">From the Torah on: God set things up <b>administered by humans to humans</b></li><li class=\"d1\">people in authority - not to <b>lord it over</b> them (as Christ points out)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>high priest</b> walked camp dressed like everyone else - <b>vestments only in the tabernacle</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"God knows how we're built\" → we need <b>someone outside ourselves</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Nothing left to <b>individual Israelites</b></li><li class=\"d1\">later period: <b>everyone does what is right in their own eyes</b> - \"really horrible time to live in Israel\"</li><li class=\"d0\">God entrusts to certain people and <b>holds them accountable</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1925.63,"lv":2,"h":"3:40-45 - Firstborn census; Levites in their place","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Census of <b>all firstborn males</b> a month old and up</li><li class=\"d1\">Levites taken <b>instead of the firstborn</b>, Levites' <b>cattle</b> instead of Israel's firstborn cattle</li><li class=\"d1\">firstborn males: <b>22,273</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Levites have <b>firstborn status</b> - Levi is <b>third</b> son, but <b>Reuben and Simeon disowned</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why they're the priests</li><li class=\"d0\">Numbers of Levite males and Israel's firstborn <b>roughly the same</b> → firstborn status goes to the Levites</li><li class=\"d1\">otherwise <b>firstborn sons would be priests</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2026.43,"lv":3,"h":"The old pattern: heads of families as priests","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Old pattern (cf. <b>golden calf</b>): <b>no priesthood per se</b></li><li class=\"d1\">sacrifices by <b>fathers of families, heads of clans</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Job</b> sacrificing for his children; <b>Abraham, Isaac, Jacob</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>firstborn son</b> inherited that role</li><li class=\"d0\">Levi as firstborn: duties <b>given to the tribe of Levi</b>, no one else</li><li class=\"d0\">Not what actually happens</li><li class=\"d1\">workarounds: <b>hiring Levites to sacrifice to idols</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Census numbers a <b>symbolic function</b> → big round numbers; precision not needed</li></ul>"},{"t":2124.44,"lv":2,"h":"3:46-51 - Redemption money","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>273</b> firstborn in excess of the Levites → <b>5 shekels each</b>, by the <b>holy shekel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">silver given to <b>Aaron and his sons</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>1,365 shekels</b> (read as \"1,375 and 65\")</li><li class=\"d0\">Origin of the <b>temple tax</b></li><li class=\"d1\">money \"not super important\" in a desert camp - \"what are you gonna do with silver?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">matters once <b>settled in the land</b> and commerce</li><li class=\"d1\">upkeep: repairs, <b>gold plating</b> - beyond in-kind food gifts to priests</li><li class=\"d1\">based on firstborn sons → <b>bigger families pay more</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2221.58,"lv":3,"h":"The temple tax abused","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"I know you're shocked\" - it gets abused</li><li class=\"d0\">Biggest abuse: <b>Jesus' earthly ministry</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>70% of Judean land</b> not owned or run by Romans belonged to the <b>high priest's family</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Romans let them run a <b>temple tax</b> → <b>deliberately overtaxed</b>, forced sales, then paid slave wages to work their own former land</li><li class=\"d0\">Contrast: later in Numbers <b>every family gets land from God</b>; Sabbath years and <b>Jubilee</b> keep it in the family</li><li class=\"d1\">high priest's family took 70%, \"probably after the other 30\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>temple destroyed</b>, \"things went very badly for them\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Originally not for <b>priests to enrich themselves</b> - for the <b>necessary life of the tabernacle</b> to keep functioning</li></ul>"}]});
